The Slash'EM dev-team are currently considering whether to integrate the
changes made in the newly released NetHack 3.4.2 into Slash'EM Vampire or
whether to continue improving the stability of Slash'EM Vampire without
making major changes and leave the NetHack 3.4.2 integration for the next
development series (which doesn't have a name yet).

If you are a Slash'EM player and have a view on whether you would want to
play Slash'EM Vampire if it was still based on the old NetHack 3.4.1
codebase then I would be very pleased to hear it.

Ideally, the discussion should take place on the slashem-devel mailing
list so that we don't clutter up rgrn and so that it doesn't become
dis-jointed.

Please send comments to slashem-devel at lists.sourceforge.net

You can read my post to slashem-devel outlining the options at:
<http://sourceforge.net/mailarchive/message.php?msg_id=5949533>

If you would like to subscribe to slashem-devel, then please go to:
<http://lists.sourceforge.net/mailman/listinfo/slashem-devel>

